==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|satet}}, {{m|enm|satyt}}, {{m|enm|saded}}. Equivalent to {{suf|en|sate|ed}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# In a state of complete and thorough [[satisfaction]]; having ones [[appetite]] fully satisfied, by having [[enough]] of something.
#* {{circa|1603}} {{w|William Shakespeare}}, ''{{w|Othello}}'', Act I scene iii<sup>[http://www.opensourceshakespeare.org/views/plays/playmenu.php?WorkID=othello]</sup>:
#*: {{...}}She must change for youth. When she is '''sated''' with his body she will find the errors of her choice.
# [[quelled|Quelled]] of thirst or hunger.

